Search Antithesis documentation

Full-text search over a local copy of the Antithesis docs, refreshed
automatically unless --offline.

Search for a page, browse the tree to find one, then show it. `sqlite` prints
the path to the local database for querying it directly.

Examples:
  snouty docs search fault injection
  snouty docs tree sdk
  snouty docs show getting_started

Add --json for machine-readable output. `search` and `tree` print JSON; the
other subcommands print text either way:
  snouty --json docs search fault injection | jq -r '.[].path'

Usage: snouty docs [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  search  Search the documentation
  tree    Print a tree of documentation paths
  show    Show full contents of a documentation page
  sqlite  Print the path to the cached SQLite database
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --offline
          Don't check for documentation updates

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --utc
          Show times in UTC instead of the local timezone

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
